From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 19:27:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2codecs: Add the driver's frame size limit to sink caps

All stateless decoders register with the same rank and a sink template
that accepts any frame size, so autoplugging takes the first decoder for
a format. On RK3568 that is the Hantro H.264 decoder, which is limited
to 1920x1088, and a 2160p stream fails with "Failed to configure H264
decoder" while rkvdec could decode it.

Query VIDIOC_ENUM_FRAMESIZES for the coded format at registration and
put the maximum width and height into the sink pad template of each
decoder and of the alpha decode bins wrapping it. The minimum stays at
1, as set_sink_fmt() accepts a coded size the driver raises. Without
the ioctl, or with discrete sizes, the template stays unrestricted.

The device keeps the caps per coded format: with a cached registry the
classes are initialised only when an element is created, after every
codec of the device has been registered.
